**Convention 1.5 (actual native lift and credited partition).** Use
exactly [GDB, Definition 12.2 and Theorem 12.3][GDB]. At each block
$v$, the three internal targets $\varepsilon,L,R$ have factor
$(0,0)$. At the terminal slot of edge $a$, the factor is $(2,1)$
for $s_a=0$ and $(1,0)$ for $s_a=1$. Each terminal reads that
edge's actual owner, including a self Read at an owner. Its total
decoder sends branch and absent to $(2,1)$. At the owner these
excluded inputs disagree with the alpha reply predicted by $(2,1)$,
so the owner equation enforces its actual binary guard.

All seven targets in $W_3$ are specified. Every solution is the
perfect height-two tree at each vertex with the four prescribed
terminal bits; conversely every edge assignment builds exactly one
such actual tuple. Owners recover the inverse. Thus the complete
native solution set is in bijection with $\mathbb F_2^E$, has
$2^{2n}$ rows, and each edge has incidence two. The equality of the
two occurrences is part of this bijection. For arbitrary nonnegative
original weights $w_v:S_3\to[0,\infty)$ its exact mass is
$\sum_s\prod_v w_v(x_v(s))$, with each $w_v$ once. In (WBF.5)
the restriction of $w_v$ to those sixteen perfect trees is $\Phi_v$;
its other values do not affect this solution set.

The credited incidence-rank and syndrome calculation [GDB, Theorem
13.1 and Corollary 13.2][GDB] gives, on this connected carrier,

$$
Z_G=2^n\big[(A+B)^n+(A-B)^n\big].
\tag{WBF.6}
$$

